1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,550
A test screening tells you the audience
got bored. It does not tell you where.

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:07,408
MomentLab answers that question with a
timestamp.

3
00:00:09,008 --> 00:00:12,456
35,001 respondents watched this scene.

4
00:00:12,456 --> 00:00:19,626
Across roughly 2 million playback events,
retention drops 18.1% at 37 seconds —

5
00:00:19,626 --> 00:00:23,074
inside a window from 33 to 41 seconds.

6
00:00:24,674 --> 00:00:29,097
Retention is aggregated per age cohort
inside ClickHouse, in an

7
00:00:29,097 --> 00:00:31,835
AggregatingMergeTree materialized view.

8
00:00:31,835 --> 00:00:35,976
The curve you're seeing came back in about
45 milliseconds.

9
00:00:35,976 --> 00:00:40,750
The same question against raw events takes
roughly three times that.

10
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:47,444
This is a Google ADK agent running Gemini
2.5 Pro on Vertex AI.

11
00:00:47,444 --> 00:00:53,993
When I re-run the analysis, it queries
ClickHouse through the official ClickHouse

12
00:00:53,993 --> 00:00:58,279
MCP server and forms a hypothesis from
what it finds.

13
00:00:59,879 --> 00:01:01,917
The indicator is not decorative.

14
00:01:01,917 --> 00:01:07,268
It reflects real service health and the
number of agent runs in the last 15

15
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:09,498
When nothing has run, it says idle.

16
00:01:11,098 --> 00:01:13,788
Every query the agent ran is recorded —

17
00:01:13,788 --> 00:01:17,236
up to 50 executions, with duration and row
counts.

18
00:01:17,236 --> 00:01:20,892
This is the agent's actual work, not a
summary of it.

19
00:01:22,492 --> 00:01:28,834
Open any one of them and you get the query
ID, the execution time, the row count,

20
00:01:28,834 --> 00:01:32,983
and the exact SQL. 3 milliseconds, 737
rows returned.

21
00:01:32,983 --> 00:01:36,820
You can verify the number instead of
trusting it.

22
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:44,628
Every figure carries its state. PREDICTED
means a forecast. MEASURED means a result.

23
00:01:44,628 --> 00:01:48,101
GROUNDED means real ClickHouse queries
back it.

24
00:01:48,101 --> 00:01:53,053
Nothing is called verified unless the
system actually confirmed it.

25
00:01:54,653 --> 00:01:57,326
The agent proposes. A person approves.

26
00:01:57,326 --> 00:02:02,812
This edit is a testable proposal with a
predicted effect and a reviewer gate —

27
00:02:02,812 --> 00:02:04,148
not an instruction.

28
00:02:05,748 --> 00:02:13,473
The cut measured an 11.1% engagement lift,
with a 95% confidence interval from

29
00:02:13,473 --> 00:02:21,792
10.9% to 11.4%, across 17,500 respondents
per arm. Only then is it labeled MEASURED.

30
00:02:23,392 --> 00:02:25,817
No cameras. No facial recognition.

31
00:02:25,817 --> 00:02:31,667
Only consented in-player reactions,
aggregated behind a minimum cohort size of

32
00:02:31,667 --> 00:02:34,092
The demo runs on a seeded dataset.

33
00:02:34,092 --> 00:02:38,158
The agent, the queries and the measurement
path are real.

34
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:43,294
A screening tells you the audience got
bored. MomentLab tells you where.
